{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>What shall I speak, and He says to me.</b> Behold me — He will add to your days." "And the word <b>עשה</b> is like יעשה, and likewise נתתי כסף השדה (Genesis 23:13). Or the sense of עשה is: He who did this kindness with me — nevertheless I will recount all my years in remembering this measure that passed over me." "And the word <b>אדדה</b> is from the nifal binyan, and it has no cognate in Scripture except אדדם עד בית אלהים (Psalms 42:5), and in the Mishnah מדדה את בנה [Shabbat 18b]. And the sense is known."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:53.574960740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}